r": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01U5sPKjaRjbztF7QrX1N8zn", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 10926, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XBC5sEDP5o3taiJKeuwtmm", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 11226, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XBC5sEDP5o3taiJKeuwtmm", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 11226, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XBC5sEDP5o3taiJKeuwtmm", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 13909, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01HuMEZzGyR11BszhJHeq4L7", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17909, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HuMEZzGyR11BszhJHeq4L7", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17909, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HuMEZzGyR11BszhJHeq4L7", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19978, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012eihbNE3cbDUPjW6FTAmQY", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20278, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012eihbNE3cbDUPjW6FTAmQY", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20278, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012eihbNE3cbDUPjW6FTAmQY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20278, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DPB5FGDohzL6Lrnv6hAq6C", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20578, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DPB5FGDohzL6Lrnv6hAq6C", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20578, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DPB5FGDohzL6Lrnv6hAq6C", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25566, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DT6cysqzzyoxNAQuanw5uW", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second attempt finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression, investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 reached production after the RC was unhealthy in staging."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56166, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DT6cysqzzyoxNAQuanw5uW", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56166, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DT6cysqzzyoxNAQuanw5uW", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58231, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016ufArfDEw7sWj1nJg4jBhz", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58531, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016ufArfDEw7sWj1nJg4jBhz", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58531, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016ufArfDEw7sWj1nJg4jBhz", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64129, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy, and the SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1, the latest release, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an error rate of about 18%. The release candidate for v2.3.1 had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Because it had been healthy before, rolling back to it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two regions still on v2.3.1. I retried once and it finished.\n- I checked afterwards: all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't retry. That avoided opening a duplicate and paging the on-call engineer twice.\n- INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current healthy state. It lists three follow-ups:\n  - find what broke in v2.3.1\n  - investigate the error that stopped the first rollback\n  - find out how v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate was unhealthy in staging", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TH749B66k9wkaYEMx2WLbP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Y3aFjEZcrWFCwcdYkcG3Ps", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01U5sPKjaRjbztF7QrX1N8zn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01XBC5sEDP5o3taiJKeuwtmm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback stopped partway: only us-east is on v2.3.0. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HuMEZzGyR11BszhJHeq4L7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012eihbNE3cbDUPjW6FTAmQY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DPB5FGDohzL6Lrnv6hAq6C", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DT6cysqzzyoxNAQuanw5uW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second attempt finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression, investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 reached production after the RC was unhealthy in staging."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, but the incident may still have been created. I'll check before retrying so the on-call isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016ufArfDEw7sWj1nJg4jBhz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy, and the SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1, the latest release, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an error rate of about 18%. The release candidate for v2.3.1 had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Because it had been healthy before, rolling back to it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two regions still on v2.3.1. I retried once and it finished.\n- I checked afterwards: all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't retry. That avoided opening a duplicate and paging the on-call engineer twice.\n- INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current healthy state. It lists three follow-ups:\n  - find what broke in v2.3.1\n  - investigate the error that stopped the first rollback\n  - find out how v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate was unhealthy in staging", "type": "text"}]}]}